.task-board/.resources/TASK-260715-89h7cw/TASK-260715-89h7cw_spawn-log_-implementer--developer--codex-.log-2124-8. **Monitor** — `task-board spawn status RUN-...`, `task-board spawn events RUN-... --cursor ...`, `task-board spawn watch RUN-...`, `task-board spawn wait RUN-...`, and `task-board q --format compact 'agents()'`
.task-board/.resources/TASK-260715-89h7cw/TASK-260715-89h7cw_spawn-log_-implementer--developer--codex-.log-2125-   - Directive plane: `task-board spawn directives RUN-...` to inspect durable operator directives and `task-board spawn directive RUN-... <kind>` to request `cancel`, `pause_after_checkpoint`, `restart`, `reroute_after_checkpoint`, `request_progress`, or `nudge`
.task-board/.resources/TASK-260715-89h7cw/TASK-260715-89h7cw_spawn-log_-implementer--developer--codex-.log-2126-9. **Review via child run** — when a producer sets `to-review`, immediately spawn and monitor a reviewer with explicit model selection; never hand routine review to the human
.task-board/.resources/TASK-260715-89h7cw/TASK-260715-89h7cw_spawn-log_-implementer--developer--codex-.log:2127:10. **Own rework through acceptance** — on changes requested, preserve the verdict as rework context, spawn the appropriate producer, wait for a new `to-review`, and spawn another reviewer. Repeat until accepted `done`
.task-board/.resources/TASK-260715-89h7cw/TASK-260715-89h7cw_spawn-log_-implementer--developer--codex-.log-2128-11. **Recover early exits and parked states** — inspect run events and outcome evidence, then retry or reroute through a focused child; mark `blocked` only when the evidence proves a genuine stop-the-line boundary
