.task-board/.resources/TASK-260715-89h7cw/TASK-260715-89h7cw_spawn-log_-implementer--developer--codex-.log-2131-Spawn is task-centric:
--
.task-board/.resources/TASK-260715-89h7cw/TASK-260715-89h7cw_spawn-log_-implementer--developer--codex-.log-2256-- **Use checklist** for tracking subtasks within a task
.task-board/.resources/TASK-260715-89h7cw/TASK-260715-89h7cw_spawn-log_-implementer--developer--codex-.log-2257-- **Bugs live in stories** — always attach to a relevant story
.task-board/.resources/TASK-260715-89h7cw/TASK-260715-89h7cw_spawn-log_-implementer--developer--codex-.log-2258-- **Sub-agents write tests** — every sub-agent is responsible for tests in its scope
.task-board/.resources/TASK-260715-89h7cw/TASK-260715-89h7cw_spawn-log_-implementer--developer--codex-.log-2259-- **Supervisor coordinates reviews** — coordinator must spawn/review-route child reviewer work before marking done
.task-board/.resources/TASK-260715-89h7cw/TASK-260715-89h7cw_spawn-log_-implementer--developer--codex-.log:2260:- **Orchestrator closes the loop** — the parent owns producer -> reviewer -> rework -> reviewer until accepted `done`; it never stops at `to-review` or asks the human to perform routine review
.task-board/.resources/TASK-260715-89h7cw/TASK-260715-89h7cw_spawn-log_-implementer--developer--codex-.log-2261-- **Visualize at milestones** — render graphs before, during, and after execution with `task-board plan --render`
.task-board/.resources/TASK-260715-89h7cw/TASK-260715-89h7cw_spawn-log_-implementer--developer--codex-.log-2262-- **Verify agents early** — run `task-board q 'agents()'` within 2 minutes of launch; if status not updated, stop and restart with better prompt
.task-board/.resources/TASK-260715-89h7cw/TASK-260715-89h7cw_spawn-log_-implementer--developer--codex-.log-2263-- **Concrete IDs only** — never use placeholders like `TASK-XXX` in prompts; always use real IDs like `TASK-260203-ae3fcd`
.task-board/.resources/TASK-260715-89h7cw/TASK-260715-89h7cw_spawn-log_-implementer--developer--codex-.log-2264-- **Human-facing references need ID + title/name** — when mentioning an epic, story, task, or bug in chat, include both so people can understand the reference without looking up the ID
.task-board/.resources/TASK-260715-89h7cw/TASK-260715-89h7cw_spawn-log_-implementer--developer--codex-.log-2265-- **No work without a task** — every code change must be tracked on the board. If a task doesn't exist, create one first. Don't start coding then retroactively create tasks
.task-board/.resources/TASK-260715-89h7cw/TASK-260715-89h7cw_spawn-log_-implementer--developer--codex-.log-2266-- **Parent is orchestrator, not worker** — the parent agent plans, creates/refines board items, spawns children, watches `RUN-...` handles, sends directives, and decides next routing. It must not do implementation, research, testing, docs, or review inline when a board task can be delegated.
.task-board/.resources/TASK-260715-89h7cw/TASK-260715-89h7cw_spawn-log_-implementer--developer--codex-.log-2267-- **Do not force-fit broken assumptions** — pause only for a concrete external blocker or an evidence-backed unresolved human-only platform/product/architecture/tradeoff/approval decision. Document the evidence, failed assumptions/attempts, viable alternatives and tradeoffs, recommendation, and exact decision or external input needed; do not build a tower of stubs, flags, priority rules, and tests around an invalid model.
.task-board/.resources/TASK-260715-89h7cw/TASK-260715-89h7cw_spawn-log_-implementer--developer--codex-.log-2268-- **All task work through tracked background spawn** — every board task MUST run in a separate CLI process with explicit `--role`, `--background`, `--model`, and Codex `--reasoning-effort`. Never use an untracked Task helper or implicit model/reasoning selection for board deliverables.
.task-board/.resources/TASK-260715-89h7cw/TASK-260715-89h7cw_spawn-log_-implementer--developer--codex-.log:2269:- **Reviews are child work too** — when work reaches `to-review`, spawn an explicitly selected reviewer child such as `task-board spawn TASK-... --role reviewer --background --agent codex --model gpt-5.6-sol --reasoning-effort max`. Route accepted work to `done` or requested changes into rework and another reviewer cycle.
.task-board/.resources/TASK-260715-89h7cw/TASK-260715-89h7cw_spawn-log_-implementer--developer--codex-.log-2270-- **`to-review` is not done** — producers must report `to-review` as "ready for review" or "handed off to review". Coordinators must not tell the human "done"/"complete"/"finished"/"final"/"готово" until a reviewer has accepted the work and the board item is actually `done`.
.task-board/.resources/TASK-260715-89h7cw/TASK-260715-89h7cw_spawn-log_-implementer--developer--codex-.log-2271-- **Coordinators track `RUN-...`, not shell jobs** — after spawning, hold onto the returned run id and drive orchestration with `task-board spawn status/events/watch/wait`. Do not rely on `&`, `nohup`, or runtime background wrappers to track completion
.task-board/.resources/TASK-260715-89h7cw/TASK-260715-89h7cw_spawn-log_-implementer--developer--codex-.log-2272-- **Drive unblocked tasks to terminal handoff** — if no objective blocker remains, the spawned worker must keep going until it has checked the relevant checklist items, attached outcome evidence, and reached its producer `end_status` (`to-review`) or exactly one reviewer verdict status (`done`, `to-dev`, `analysis`, or evidence-backed `blocked`). If a child exits early or leaves a task parked in `analysis`, `development`, `testing`, or `reviewing`, retry or reroute through a focused child. Use `blocked` only for an evidence-backed external blocker or unresolved human-only stop-the-line decision, with the full evidence packet and exact human decision or external input needed to resume.
.task-board/.resources/TASK-260715-89h7cw/TASK-260715-89h7cw_spawn-log_-implementer--developer--codex-.log-2273-- **Dependent children are sequenced** — if child B consumes or reviews child A's output, the parent must `spawn wait` child A, inspect status/outcome resources, and only then spawn child B. Parallel fan-out is only for independent tasks.
--
