.task-board/.resources/TASK-260715-89h7cw/TASK-260715-89h7cw_spawn-log_-implementer--developer--codex-.log-5265-- FIX: Swift and Go now derive every local-only `RelayEffectiveLimits` field as `min(generated peer default or fixed constant, injected config)`. Lower injected caps remain effective, while valid above-default configuration cannot raise the immutable generation snapshot; negotiated `effectiveMaxFrame` remains independent.
.task-board/.resources/TASK-260715-89h7cw/TASK-260715-89h7cw_spawn-log_-implementer--developer--codex-.log-5266-- FIX: Both incremental state machines classify a full or partial generated `RLXR` prefix already present after the accepted hello in the same callback as `duplicateHello` before publishing success, while preserving legal coalesced hello-plus-frame input.
.task-board/.resources/TASK-260715-89h7cw/TASK-260715-89h7cw_spawn-log_-implementer--developer--codex-.log-5267-- DECISION: A callback ending at the exact 12/16-byte hello boundary publishes success immediately. `RLXR` first observed in a subsequent read is post-handshake input owned by `TASK-260715-1jvgcn`; the session/envelope layer must map it to a stable privacy-safe session-close reason. No lookahead, delay, or transport barrier is added.
.task-board/.resources/TASK-260715-89h7cw/TASK-260715-89h7cw_spawn-log_-implementer--developer--codex-.log-5268-- COVERAGE: Swift `perform` tests now inject invalid/throwing writes, throwing reads, and EOF, assert stable code/phase mappings, and prove cancel/reset/close cleanup. Full validation passes: `make relay-protocol-check` (19 selected protocol tests), `swift test` (129/129), Go vet/test with `CGO_ENABLED=0` and 92.6% statement coverage, strict Swift format, gofmt, core-boundary check, `git diff --check`, and board validation.
